           "short": "14 terms.",
           "worked": "$a=\\frac32$, $d=\\frac12$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{133}{2}&=\\frac{n}{2}\\left[2\\left(\\frac32\\right)+(n-1)\\frac12\\right]\\\\\\frac{133}{2}&=\\frac{n}{2}\\cdot\\frac{n+5}{2}\\\\266&=n(n+5)\\\\n^2+5n-266&=0\\\\(n-14)(n+19)&=0\\\\n&=14\\text{ or }-19\\end{align*}$$\nSince $n>0$, 14 terms are needed."
          }
         },
         {
          "id": "v2-proposal-j6-082703-j6-gp-c",
          "type": "part",
          "label": "c",
          "prompt": "$-12-9-6+\\cdots$ where $S_n=54$",
          "answerSpaceMm": 55,
          "answer": {
           "short": "12 terms.",
           "worked": "$a=-12$, $d=3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}54&=\\frac{n}{2}[2(-12)+(n-1)3]\\\\108&=n(3n-27)\\\\n^2-9n-36&=0\\\\(n-12)(n+3)&=0\\\\n&=12\\text{ or }-3\\end{align*}$$\nSince $n>0$, 12 terms are needed."
          }
